id: pm-vcs-rd82
title: Keep test children from delivering pm telemetry and Sentry reports
description: "test/served-defects.test.ts labelled its installed-CLI children PM_TELEMETRY_SOURCE_CONTEXT=test (plus PM_TELEMETRY_INLINE_FLUSH=1) to avoid the detached flusher. Under pm-cli's documented policy a valid explicit source-context label permits intentional test delivery even under NODE_ENV=test, so the suite's expected vcs fetch/push/clone/remote refusals reached the production Sentry project as ExtensionCommandError (environment=test). CI runs on 2026-11-04 00:26-03:45Z created PM-CLI-3R, 3S, 3T, 3V, 3W and 3X, which blocked pm-cli's Auto Release Sentry gate for 2026.11.4 (pm-cli#1659). GitHub: unbraind/pm-vcs#176."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: ci,sentry,telemetry,testing
created_at: "2026-11-04T09:51:28.097Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-04T10:43:42.513Z"
assignee: claude-hub
claim_principal: claude-hub
author: claude-hub
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "testEnvironment() adds the hard opt-out PM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1, which no source-context label or PM_TELEMETRY_SEND_TEST_EVENTS overrides; served-defects drops the label; a regression test routes the event endpoint and SENTRY_DSN to a local collector, proves the route before any delivery-capable command, and shows a labelled child reports telemetry disabled and sends zero requests, failing when the opt-out is removed."
severity: high
expected_result: No test child process delivers telemetry events or Sentry reports to production collectors.
component: test/helpers
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-04T10:43:42.513Z",claude-hub,"Verified 2026-11-04 on pm-cli 2026.10.30. The regression passes with the fix. With PM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED removed from testEnvironment it fails: a labelled child reports enabled=true, and its requests reach only the local collector. Experiment with the old served-defects env: one failing pm get produced 3 POST /v1/events to the local collector, and 0 with PM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1. Trap: a project settings telemetry.endpoint is ignored; only the global profile under PM_GLOBAL_PATH is honored, so the test proves the route before any delivery-capable command (filed upstream as pm-cli#1660). All 18 test files that spawn the installed pm CLI pass: 420/420. served-defects passes for node and bun. test-environment.test.ts 6/6. typecheck, lint, docstring and duplicates pass."
files[3]{path,scope,note}:
  test/helpers/test-environment.ts,project,hard telemetry opt-out for every test child
  test/served-defects.test.ts,project,drops the delivery-permitting label
  test/test-environment.test.ts,project,local-collector regression
tests[1]{command,scope,timeout_seconds,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref},note}:
  node --test --test-name-pattern='deliver no pm telemetry' test/test-environment.test.ts,project,300,claude-hub,"2026-11-04T09:51:31.652Z",local_mutation,fix/test-children-never-deliver-telemetry,labelled child sends nothing to a local collector
body: ""
